<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Jewish–Roman War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">66–73</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Great Jewish Revolt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Jewish–Roman War was the revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a> against Roman rule from 66 to 73 CE. Vespasian and then his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus">Titus</a> reconquered the province; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> fell after a long siege in 70 CE and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a> was destroyed, and the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masada">Masada</a> was taken in 73 or 74. The war is described in detail by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephus">Josephus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war.jpg" alt="First Jewish–Roman War" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: בית השלום · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arch_of_Titus_Menorah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
